1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,400
Burp Suite Enterprise Edition offers a number of site-related settings that enable you to

2
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:15,040
fine-tune Burp Scanners' behaviour and provide additional information such as login credentials.

3
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:20,560
You can access these settings from the Scan Settings panel, either during the process of

4
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:26,960
creating a site as we are now, or while editing an existing site. The following tabs are available.

5
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:33,760
First, we have the Scan Configuration tab, which enables you to specify one or more configurations

6
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:40,080
to use when scanning the site. We have two options using a preset scan mode or a custom configuration.

7
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:45,920
If you'd like to learn more about scan configuration options, please see our documentation

8
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:53,600
defining scan configurations for a site. Next, we have Application Logins. This enables you to provide

9
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:59,040
login credentials for the site, and we have two options, the first of which is adding usernames

10
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:05,040
and passwords or uploading a recorded login sequence. If you'd like to learn more about

11
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:10,480
application logins for sites, please see our documentation configuring site login details.

12
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:17,440
Next, we have Extensions. This enables you to select any extensions that Burp Suite Enterprise

13
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:22,800
Edition should use when scanning the site. To learn more about this, please see our documentation

14
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:30,320
scanning with extensions. Next, we have Scanning Pool, which enables you to select a scanning pool for

15
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:36,160
the site to belong to. If you'd like to learn more about scanning pools, please see our documentation

16
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:42,720
managing scanning pools. And finally, we have Scan Notifications. This enables you to configure

17
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:48,640
automated notifications on Scan Progress. To learn how to set this up, please see our documentation

18
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:55,280
setting up Scan Notifications. Please note you must select a scan configuration in order to be able to

19
00:01:55,280 --> 00:02:10,160
save the site. All of the settings in the Scan Settings section are optional. Thank you.

